<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $10.8 mln in Oct 21 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $10.8 mln in Oct 21 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $10.8 billion in the Oct 21 week to $3,779.8 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $14.7 billion to $4,819.4 billion.</p>
<p>M-1 rose $11.4 billion to $1,080.2 billion.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,768.4 billion versus $3,763.2 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>--N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
